0..94 Comment "// One function of a buddy allocator, popping a free block, meets its free-list specification."
95..97 Comment "//"
98..320 Comment "// Corten\'s case study verifies a buddy allocator against a representation predicate over Rust\'s value forest. This is its second rung after Corten\'s `example`, a function that reads, matches on and writes through a place."
321..323 Comment "//"
324..633 Comment "// The body is THIR written as data, its precondition computed by a weakest-precondition fold over it. A read or a write is an existential, a value the place holds with its equation, so stuck places stay in path endpoints. The proof cases on the free list and carries each equation by `Path.ap` and transport."
634..636 Comment "//"
637..706 Comment "// - see: Farka et al., Corten, arXiv:2609.04372, 2026, § 3 and § 8"
707..756 Comment "// - see: corpus/model/interop/thir/example.gandr"
758..767 Comment "// `Nat`."
